<h2>Asobi Review 0.2 (build 494)</h2>
<p><b>Print-film looks now apply the way Resolve applies them.</b></p>
<ul>
<li><b>Film Lab looks apply after the display transform</b>, on display-referred picture — the standard placement for a print emulation, and how a 2383 PFE sits in a Resolve node tree. Previously the look ran before the tonemap, in scene space, where everything above diffuse white fell outside the LUT's range: 2 stops over and 4 stops over both flattened to one value, below diffuse white. Measured now: highlights stay graded and monotonic at every strength — 2-over and 4-over land at distinct values with the print shoulder intact.</li>
<li><b>Strength blends cleanly at any setting.</b> Halfway between no look and the full print, instead of blending against a clipped image.</li>
<li><b>Looks will render slightly differently than before</b> — denser, more print-like in the mids, with highlights that keep their gradation. That is the placement change doing its job; recipes and saved looks are unchanged and re-render through the new placement automatically. Look chips re-render to match.</li>
<li>This applies to Film Lab looks — live and saved ones (recognized by the recipe file saved beside the cube). Library LUTs that declare their own working spaces (camera-log print LUTs and the like) are already in their right place and are untouched.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
